# NOTE: MSan does NOT support runtime suppression files.
# The 'suppressions=' key is not recognized by MSAN_OPTIONS and will produce
# a "WARNING: found 1 unrecognized flag(s): suppressions" message if used.
#
# False positives from uninstrumented prebuilt libraries (libnode.so, libpython.so)
# are handled at runtime via:
#   MSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=0:exit_code=0
# which prevents test processes from aborting when MSan reports errors
# originating inside uninstrumented shared libraries.
#
# For compile-time suppression of sources that are built with MSan instrumentation
# (e.g. GoogleTest), use the -fsanitize-ignorelist flag pointing to msan-ignorelist.txt.
